{"id": "EUVD-2026-90656", "enisaUuid": "4076c0ac-9a5d-33ac-9a37-9cf38f2ee8c6", "description": "Tornado versions before 6.5.9 contain an unbounded memory accumulation vulnerability in CurlAsyncHTTPClient that allows remote attackers to cause denial of service by sending a compressed response. Attackers can send a gzip-encoded decompression bomb that accumulates in memory without size limits, causing the application process to be killed by out-of-memory conditions.", "datePublished": "2026-10-01T10:42:04", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-06T00:08:58", "baseScore": 8.7, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/security/advisories/GHSA-chx6-46f5-w4vp", "https://github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/commit/e412435febba4569c552c5c9054f1bf92bd171a9", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/tornado-before-6.5.9-denial-of-service-via-curlasynchttpclient"], "aliases": ["GHSA-h36x-fm6v-f9vx", "CVE-2026-103262"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.52, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "cba8b01d-2f9a-385f-a858-578329a51cc3", "product": {"name": "Tornado", "vendor": {"name": "tornadoweb"}}, "product_version": "0 <6.5.9"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "1d30bb83-ae43-3e52-a270-d2209e9ae72e", "vendor": {"name": "tornadoweb"}}], "isExploited": false}